All three functions are implemented and `python3 test_impl.py` now prints `ALL PASS` (stress loop took 3.0s). I ran the suite after each function, and `test_impl.py` is untouched.

- **`encode`** in `rle.py`: groups consecutive characters and emits each character followed by its run length.
- **`decode`** in `rle.py`: reads each non-digit character plus the digits after it and expands the run.
- **`merge`** in `intervals.py`: sorts by start and folds each interval into the previous one when it overlaps or touches. It returns new lists, so the input isn't mutated.

One limitation follows from the format in the docstring: a string that itself contains digits (e.g. `"11"` encodes to `"12"`) won't round-trip through `decode`. The tests don't exercise this.
